title: Feil
position: 2,-179
---
<<set $affection = 0>>
<<Swap Observatory>>
The observatory has a subtle fragrance of old paper and coffee. 
A single beam of moonlight shines through the skylight,[br /]and the air is filled with the quiet hum of machines. 
Feil the Grass-Wrighthumb stands at the telescope,[br /]moving dials about with an excessive flourish. 
He loudly clears his throat,[br /]and the light from the stars shines on his glasses.
<<Animate RTIdle>>

Feil: "Look up," he says in a deep, rich voice.
Feil:"Every star you see has been burning for millions, and sometimes billions, of years.
Feil: But here you are, looking at them alongside me. A strange coincidence, or maybe even an inevitability.”
Feil: “I am Feil the Grass-Wrighthumb, a galaxy explorer, a debunker of pseudoscience,[br /]and maybe even the smartest thumb in the room. 
Feil: But enough about me... what draws you to the stars?“
->I know very little about stars but I know that they are truly breathtaking.
    <<set $affection +=1>>
    Feil: “A mind that is open to the universe is... magnetic. 
    Feil: I feel like I'm being sucked into your orbit, like gravity. 
    Feil: Be careful, I might classify you as a celestial body.”
->Stars? Those are just little lights in the sky.. They don’t affect me.
    <<set $affection -=1>>
    Feil:“You’ve just committed a cosmic crime of underestimation! They are so much more than what the eyes can see.”
->I want to better understand them and our place in this journey we call life. Not like those dumb-ass Yale folks who just romanticize them.
    <<set $affection +=2>>
    Feil: “A true visionary! You’re way of thinking is music to my ears. To be honest, if I had to make a choice between those Yale star gazers and your eyes.. Well, Yale just never stood a chance.”

Feil: “When we gaze up into the night sky, we’re not just looking out into the cosmos.. We’re looking back into past. Some of the stars we see in the sky have already deceased, however the light still travels it’s way to us. It’s almost as if the cosmos itself can’t let go. Now tell me.. What does that make you feel?”
->“I feel small.. but in a weirdly positive way! I feel like I’m apart of something greater than myself”
    Feil: “That’s it! Having humility in the face of infinity.. Now that truly captivates me. For you are not just a drop in the ocean, you’re the ripple that’s caught my eye.”
    <<set $affection +=1>>
->“Makes me feel like none of this really matters, and we all just end up as dust in the end.”
    Feil: “Stardust… yes. However, you’re missing the point! To dismiss all of reality is also the same as dismissing yourself. You’d do better to try and shine brighter than any dust cloud I’ve measured.”
    <<set $affection -=1>>
->“This makes me feel more interconnected with world around me. Light that has travled across time and space was destined to meet my eyes here with you.”
    Feil: “Now that is some fascinating cosmic thinking. You’ve turned astrophysics into a romance, and I’ll admit it – you outplayed me here. You be careful or I might just go and start charting a new constellation in your honor.”
    <<set $affection +=2>>

Feil: “Starlight can take millions of years to reach our eyes' gaze. It’s as if the universe is reaching, trying to grab your attention. I now find myself doing the same exact thing… but now I’d like to know, what deserves your attention more: yourself or the stars?”
->“I couldn’t compare. I really just blend in with the masses.”
    <<set $affection -=1>>
    Feil: “Such a tragedy of self-perception and reflection! Even a black hole has some swagger.”
->“There’s no comparison to be made. The stars shine way brighter than little old me.”
    Feil: “As impressive as they are, they can’t hold a conversation. Nor do they have the ability to make me laugh. You honestly need to give yourself some credit.”
    <<set $affection -=1>>
->“You kidding me? The stars never even stood a chance! They might light up our night’s sky but I’m lighting up this moment!”
    Feil: “Oh-hoh-hoh! A response on par with a supernova! I’d better calm down before I make you my personal big bang.
    <<set $affection +=1>>

Feil: “Every time I gaze up at the stars, I can’t help but wonder… with the billions of galaxies, each containing billions of stars, with numerous planets orbiting them. How can we possibly be alone? Truthfully, do you believe sentient life exists beyond our speck in the universe?”
->“There has to be! Our universe is too boundless for it to be just us.”
    Feil: “I had a feeling that'd be your response. Your mind is open, expansive… like the cosmos itself. If I ever found life out there in the great beyond, I’d hope it was at least half as intriguing as the life beside me now.”
    <<set $affection +=1>>
->“I don’t know if life is out there, but I’d hate to be the first to find out… They could be dangerous.”
    Feil: “Dangerous? Oh, I don’t doubt it. Encountering new life might feel less like a handshake and more like… dropping into a hostile hellscape with never-ending swarms of man-eating insects. But that’s the price we must pay for DEMOCRACY!!
    Feil: (*coughs*) “ahem… I mean discovery. And if I ever charge headfirst into the unknown, I’d want you there, covering my back.”
    <<set $affection +=1>>
->“Yeah, fat chance there’s life out there pal. The stars are just little sky ornaments… nothing special.”
