title: PennyRP
position: 17,-22
---
<<set $affection = 0>>
<<Swap Waterpark>>
Background: The fluorescent lights flicker like they’re on their last legs, casting half-shadows across the tiled bathroom. The scent of chlorine and lemon cleaner hangs thick in the air—unmistakably the smell of a waterpark after hours.
Background: Through the walls, you can hear the faint hum and rush of water slides and fountains still running in the otherwise empty Tinkle Town Water Park. The echo makes the silence of the bathroom feel even louder.

//Intro Dialogue

Player (to themselves) :Great… locked in the bathroom after hours… in Tinkle Town of all places.
Player (to themselves):Perfect… *long sigh*
You rattle the door's handle again to no avail and start banging on the door.
Player: HELLO!?!?!
Player: IS ANYONE THERE!?!
Player: I NEED HELP… I’M TRAPPED IN HERE!!
Dead silence, you couldn’t even hear a pin drop.
You take a long, deep breath and prepare to kick down the door.
Player: AAAAHHHH!!!
Just as your foot hits the door with all of your weight and strength behind it… the lock clicks open.
The door BLASTS outward at an unforgiving speed and nails someone directly on the other side.
<<Animate RPIdle>>
Penny: EEIIGHHHHH!?!
Player: HOOLLLYYY SHHHIIIITTTT?!?
You watch in slow-motion horror as a pointer finger dressed as a lifeguard is airborne and being launched back to the swimming area…
The door swings closed, and in that instance, you hear a loud SMACK!
You force the door open and see the pointer finger unconscious and slowly rolling into the pool.

//Dialogue Choices For Interaction 1:

//Choice 1 (+): 
->Rush to her aid and pull her out of the pool.
    She sinks into the pool as you rush into action.
    You dive in after her, pulling up and out of the water.
    She’s unconscious still and you notice… SHE ISN’T BREATHING!
    You prepare to start CPR even though you have little to no idea what you’re doing.
    Just as you're about to start, she wakes up and clocks you with an uppercut. Sending you flying onto your back.
    Penny: WHOOTH THA FUCK ARE YOU?!
    Your laying down on your back still in a daze and you bit your tongue when she layed you out.
    Player: I’M THO THORRY! *wincing in pain*
    Player: I wath tha one who wath trapped in tha bathroom.
    Penny glares at you, arms crosses, still dripping water on the floor.
    Penny: THO! You’re tha one who flung tthhat door at me! I thought you wereth a prankther trying to thabotage my thlide.
    Player: No! I wath just trapped in the bathroom… I wath juth trying to help!
    Penny blinks at you, her foot tapping the wet tiles rapidly, impatient rhythms, like a metronome set to “danger”.
    Penny: Hmph…
    Penny: Thith… Thith I can deal with. But next time, DON’T FLING DOORTH AT ME! I needth to protect tha thlides, and I can’t do that if I’m dead!
    Penny’s chest rises and falls in sharp, irritated breaths. Water drips off her lifeguard whistle like it’s judging you too.
    Player: I’m thorry.. *cough*
    The swelling from biting your tongue starts to fade
    Player: I meant to say, I’m sorry... I really wasn’t messing with the slides though, I promise.
    Penny narrows her gaze at you, her foot tapping faster.
    She suddenly stops.
    Penny: Hmph. Fine. Jutht… don’t do anything thtupid again. You almotht gave me a heart attack AND a concuthion.
    She adjusts her small red lifeguard floatie strapped to her back, still giving you an intense glare.
    Penny: Now the real question ith.. Why were even in the bathroom AFTER hourth!?
//Goes into Intercation #2

//Choice 2 (☠️): 
->Look for a way out of Tinkle Town Water Park.
    You freeze for a moment, watching on at the pointer finger slowly but surely sinking into the pool.
    You don’t even think about saving her, you just don’t want to be caught trespassing in the park after hours. That really made your stomach twist into knots… not the fact that you might’ve just killed someone.
    After around an hour of searching you find an exit, but there’s a security guard just on the other side of the door…
    //SUB Choice 1(+☠️): 
    ->Another kick should do the trick
        You glare at the security guard through the glass door, and you know the one thing that’s worked well for you tonight.
        Kicking things really, really hard.
        You take some steps back then beat your chest hard a couple times, hyping yourself up.
        The guard slowly starts turning around to see what animal is lurking behind him.
        The guard’s confused expression turns into pure fear and dread as he see’s you in a fall charge heading for the door, then…
        BAAMMMM!! CRASH!!!
        The door proceeds to fly off its hinges, taking the guard with it as glass spatters all over the pavement.
        After a few seconds of flight, the guard and door are launched a few feet back and then smack onto the pavement.
        You start to cackle under your breath
        Player:THAT’S WHY WE DON’T SKIP LEG DAY SON! HA HA!
        You continue your escape by carjacking a nearby van filled with senior citizens and drive off.
        [Years Later]
        You’ve built a life for yourself, a peaceful one.
        You almost forgot about the waterpark
        You almost forgot about the guard
        And you most definitely forgot about the unconscious pointer finger you let slide into the pool.
        However, Karma has a way of sneaking up on you.
        One day you receive a fateful knock on your door.
        It’s the police, with the kind of grim and unforgiving expressions usually reserved for murderers and psychopaths.
        Police:We’ve got some questions for ya…
        Police:it’s about Tinkle Town Water Park.
        They proceed to layout all the evidence they’ve got against you. 
        They show you the security footage in the water park, and in the parking lot.
        They also made sure you got to see your legendary kicks in action.
        What you didn’t know was that your legendary kicks were a bit too legendary. They actually killed both Penny and the guard stationed at the door.
        You never even had a chance to defend yourself and the case went viral across all major news stations.
        You are sentenced to death by the state, and live out your few remaining days locked up in a maximum security prison.
        But man, those were some nice kicks weren’t they.
        [GAME OVER:“FAILED ESCAPE” ☠️]
        <<jump Menu>>
    //SUB Choice 2(💀): 
    ->Try to sneak past
        You sneak as quietly as you possibly can, holding you’re breath and concentrating on every step.
        The guard doesn’t even blink… because he’s been genuinely confused of what you’re trying to do, he’s been watching you make a fool of yourself the entire time.
        Guard:What in the hell are you doing?!
        Guard:Only an absolute freak would be camping in a water park of all places… GET YOUR ASS OVER NOW!!!
        You’re now taken into police custody and are taken into the park’s office, where they also discover the surveillance footage of your “incident”.
        You’re charged with involuntary manslaughter and trespassing, and now you get to spend some years in a local state penitentiary to reflect on your actions. 
        [GAME OVER:CAUGHT ☠️]
        <<jump Menu>>
    //SUB Choice 3(💀): 
    ->Try to bribe him
        You dig through your pockets and offer the guard three nickels and a dime.
        He looks at you for a moment
        Then looks at the change in your misfigured hand
        He then looks back at you, his expression concerned
        Guard:It’s ok pal, no need to be worried… Did you loose you’re care taker?
        The guard genuinely believes you are senile.
        Guard:Don’t you worry now, just come with me and we’ll get you sorted out.
        Before you can even get a word out, he gently guides you into a bright pastel van parked nearby.
        The van smells like lavender and old disinfectant that leaves an unsettling taste in your mouth. You’re surrounded by a grumpy group of seniors.
        The van gradually starts to pull away, the guard smiles at you and you begin to realize that your daring “escape” has ended… not in freedom, but at the Sunset Serenity Home for the Easily Confused.
        [GAME OVER:“RETIRED”☠️]
        <<jump Menu>>

//Dialogue Choices For Interaction 2:
Her gaze intensifies even more, tracking all of your body’s movements.
Penny:And don’t even try lying.
Penny:(*In a Liam Neeson “Taken” voice*) I CAN THMELL FEAR…

//Choice 1 (☠️): 
->Lie.
    Player:I was trapped… I can’t lie about that.
    Player:But also… I’m actually the, uh…
    Player:The Official Tinkle Town SAFETY INSPECTOR!
    Penny freezes, her whistle stops mid-jiggle. A single drop of water freezes on her lifeguard vest like someone just clicked pause on her reality.
    …The what?
    Player:The Safety inspector! I inspect… the slides, pipes, and the bathrooms… for safety things!
    Penny:Really… Really?
    She hustles away into an office and comes back with a clipboard.
    Penny:Then I’d like you to tell me… who ith thith?
    On the clipboard is a photo of the real safety inspector: It’s a bald man with no teeth… except for one lonely yellow fang. His eyes are bloodshot and one of his eyes seems to be permanently locked onto the floor. 
    Penny:You thee thith guy?
    Penny:That’s our safety inspector. Used to be a heavy crack addict.
    Penny:Now you’re telling me… that you’re this guy?
    Player:Uhhh… well… I mean… I–
    Penny narrows her eyes into your very soul. She’s trembling with judgement.
    Penny:I KNEW I THMELLED FEAR FROM YOU!?!
    She then takes off her small lifeguard floatie and hooks you around the neck with it.
    Penny:GET OVER HERE!
    She yanks you towards her, choking you out in the process, then follows up the attack with a devastating right hook to the jaw.
    As your consciousness slowly fades… you hear Penny mutter one last thing.
    Penny:How’th the floor tathe… Bithch.
    [GAME OVER:LIAR☠️]
    <<jump Menu>>

//Choice 2 (+): 
->Tell her the truth.
    Player:I was trapped in there… I was doom scrolling for a couple of hours and someone must’ve accidentally locked me in.
    Player:So I kinda panicked and in a last-ditch effort… I, uhhh.. kicked the door really hard. 
    Player:I really wasn’t trying to hurt you... I was just desperate to get out, I swear.
    Penny eyes you up and down, judging your response.
    Penny:Hmph…
    Penny:The truth cometh out. I apprethiate the hon-ethty.
    She exhales, the tension from the situation slowly starts to dissipate. She’s still dripping water and is a bit intimidating, but now… she’s slightly less murderous.
    //Goes into Interaction #3


//Dialogue Choices For Interaction 3 (Final Interaction):

Penny:Ttho... you swear you weren’t going to thabotage my thlides?
Player:No! I swear! I was literally just… trapped.
She then picks up a small and soggy lifeguard vest, it just barely covers your chest. It smells like mold and chlorine.
Penny:Okay… thine. I believe you.
Penny:But you’re NOT getting off so easy. You almotht KILLED me!
Penny:If ya help me check on all the thlides, maybe I’ll let ya oth the hook.
Player:Got it! I’ll do my best to help in whatever way I can!
Penny grins a little, though it looks more like a predator enjoying a slightly confused snack than anything friendly. You, however, feel like you just dodged a hurricane disguised as a finger.
:You follow Penny as she does numerous routine checks, you kind of just stand there most of time taking in all the weird and surprising information about slide maintenance. She then marches you to the top of Tinkle Town’s largest attraction: THE GOLDEN TORRENT.
It spirals down three stories into a yellowish-colored pool.
Penny:Alright. Lithen up, rookie.
Penny:Thith thlide is our biggith attraction here, ttho we can’th metthh thith up.
Penny:I need you to twith the launch valve while I go thecure the landing thone.
Player:The launch valve?
Penny:YETH! The big RED one.
Penny:DO! NOT! TOUTHH! ANYTHING ELTH!
Penny:Got it?
Player:I got it!
She quickly slides along the rail of the stairway, making her way to the landing zone.
Penny:(*From Below*) OKAY! TWIST THE VALVE!
Oh and by the way… You’re totally color blind. You really should’ve mentioned that. Good Luck! 😈

//Choice 1 (+): 
->Twist the Muted Colored Valve
    You remember Penny’s instructions and lock in.
    You slowly turn the Muted Colored Valve, and touch nothing else.
    Penny:YOU DID IT! GREAT JOB UP THERE!
    You twist the valve back into it’s original positon and make your way down back to Penny.
    Penny:We could hath a real problem on our handth if you messed with other valve.
    Before you could even react, she plants a quick kiss on your cheek.
    Penny:Don’t get cocky… improper uthe of thlides can cauthe real harm. But you did a good job today, rookie.
    You survived Penny Pointerson… and somehow, she’s impressed.
    [SUCESSFUL ROMANCE ENDING: SLIDE CERTIFIED ❤️]
    <<jump Menu>>
	
//Choice 2 (☠️): 
->Twist the Muted Green Valve
    Player:It’s for sure this one… I think?
    Famous Last Words…
    You twisted the incorrect valve.
    The pipes leading to the valve start to hiss loudly as the pressure within them starts to increase.
    Penny:(*In a terrified/trembling tone*) What hath you done, you fool…
    Suddenly, the facility erupts into chaos. Pipes burst with a deafening roar, spraying water in every direction.
    One pipe, meant to regulate water temperature, shatters, spewing a scalding, flammable liquid.
    Sparks from a metal bolt ignite the substance, turning the pipe into an impromptu flamethrower, shooting fire across the room.
    Flames roar and scalding liquid hisses across the floor, engulfing everything in chaos.
    As the inferno reaches Penny, she doesn’t even scream. She just locks her eyes onto you with a fury that no mere mortal could comprehend, she’s then swallowed by the fire and smoke.
    You, however make your way to the very top of The Golden Torrent. Covering your face with the small life vest to avoid breathing in the overcrowding smoke.
    The chaos roars below, but you hear a distant whop of a helicopter blades that cuts through the roar.
    You’ve made it to the top, completely out of breath and a little singed from the flames. Just in time the rescuers from the helicopter break through the skylight and pick you up from the top of the slide just as the facility starts to crumble down.
    You’ve managed to escape the chaos of your own creation, while Penny becomes yet another casualty of your misadventure.
    Your also now paranoid that Penny will get her revenge from beyond the grave.
    [GAME OVER: BAD ENDING]
    <<jump Menu>>

===
title: PhilipRM
position: 14,151
---
Narrator: The alley stretches like a forgotten scar between two crumbling brick buildings. Graffiti completely covers the walls: incoherent gang tags, some weird political cartoons, and what seems to be a really graphic Rule 34-type scenario going on with Mario doing something with a pineapple… 

Narrator: Luckily it’s mostly covered up by the other tags. 

Narrator: However, you notice something scribbled on Mario’s pineapple.

Narrator: It’s a message in a really detailed script handwriting with a number written below. The message reads…

Narrator: “Call me with your best Chewbacca impression: (123)-FLIP-(4567).”

//Background Interaction 1:

//Choice 1 (⚪): 
->You have to make that call.😂
    Narrator: You get your phone out and immediately dial the number.
    Narrator: You take a second to cough and hype yourself up to make your best possible impression as you wait for someone to answer your call…
    Bar Phone: Ello? This is Flip’s… whatcha want, mate?
    Narrator: There’s a long pause…
    Bar Phone: Ell–
    Player: (*Very Loudly*) RAWRRWWGGHHH-ARRR!!
    Narrator: The voice on the line is silent for a moment…
    Narrator: Then…
    Bar Phone: AAGHHHH!! BLOODY HELL!?! WHAT THE F—?!
    Narrator: You hear the phone drop and tumble on the floor… you then hear a very faint voice in the background.
    Bar Phone: (*Timidly*) I think I shat myself… 
    Narrator: You can’t help but burst with laughter, (I’m assuming… the writer is trying his best) as you make your way further down the alley.
//Choice 2 (⚪): 
->Too old for prank calls.
    Narrator: You roll your eyes, deciding that it would be wrong to call someone you don’t know.
    Narrator: You wouldn’t even be able to see the number anyway since your eyesight is starting to fail you.
    Narrator: Because you're old…
    Narrator: Boomer.
    Narrator: You hobble your way further down the alley, with your weak-ass knees…

Narrator: The alley smells of rain-soaked asphalt, old beer, and a faint metallic tang. A dented dumpster buzzes quietly with flies, making it clear this isn’t a place you’d stumble into by choice.
Narrator: At the far end, a flickering neon sign shows a round-faced man resembling Kim Jong Un, frozen mid–middle finger, with a few roosters behind him. The sign reads “Flip the Bird Pub”, and its glow pulses…. Menacingly…
Narrator: Beneath it, a dented and rusted metal door leans against the wall, paint peeling in curls. This place only opens from midnight to 4 a.m., tucked away from the city and common sense.
Narrator: You walk up to the door and grab the rust-stained handle and give it a tug.
Narrator: It doesn’t move.
Narrator: You give it a push… Still nothing.
Narrator: The door has been sealed shut with years of rain, rust, and complete neglect. It clearly hasn’t been opened by anyone in a very, very long time.
Narrator: For some unknown reason, maybe fate, alcoholism, or maybe just stubbornness…
Narrator: YOU decide; this is definitely the place to get that drink you’ve been craving.
Narrator: It’s not like there’s a cleaner, normal bar just around the corner.
Narrator: No! This rusted, sealed-off death trap of a door is absolutely the place to get a drink.
Narrator: You take a couple steps back and ready yourself…



//Background Interaction 2: 

//Choice 1 (⚪): 
->KICK IT!
    Narrator: You charge with all your might and BLAST kick the door open.
    Narrator: You then realize that you might’ve overdone it, as the momentum from your charge sends you tumbling down the seemingly hidden steps.
//Choice 2 (⚪): 
->SHOULDER RAM!
    Narrator: You brace your shoulder and charge full force into the door.
    Narrator: The door EXPLODES inward with a high pitched deafening SKREEECH! Announcing your arrival…
    Narrator: The impact throws you forward, and you tumble down the seemingly hidden steps.

Narrator: THUD. THUD. THUD. You finally hit the sticky floor of the pub.
Narrator: A pair of snake boots enters your view as you start recovering from your fall.
<<Animate RMIdle>>
Philip: …Crikey… that’s a new way in. Are you alright there, mate?
Narrator: You’re still in a daze and struggling to get up.
Philip: (Mildly Concerned) Here, take me hand, mate.
Narrator: Philip puts down one of the two beers he’s been holding on the bar and reaches his hand out towards you.
Narrator: You take Philip’s hand; his grip is steady and firm as he slowly pulls you upright. Whatever was on the floor is now stained all over your clothes, but you’re standing… barely.
Narrator: A sharp twinge shoots through your lower back, making you wince and lean against the bar for support.
Player: (wincing in pain) Damn… my back… think I might’ve tweaked it a little.
Philip: (cheerfully) But you're on your feet, mate! The name’s Philip, here’s a bit of medicine for ya, mate.





Dialogue Choices For Interaction 1:

//Choice 1(+): 
->Thanks (Take the Beer)
    Narrator: You take the beer. Philip smiles, lifts the other beer he’s been holding, and gives you a little nod.
    Philip: Cheers! To entering the unknown, mate!
    Narrator: You raise your beer to meet his, clinking bottles with a satisfying clink.
    Narrator: Together, you both take a deep drink, the cold, foamy liquid washing away the chaos of your alleyway entrance.
    Narrator: You take a seat at the bar and are glad that you decided to stick with this place.
//Choice 2(-): 
->I don’t drink
    Narrator: Philip’s grin fades into a sly, mocking smirk.
    Philip: Oh, so you only drink virgin stuff, do ya?
    Narrator: Philip quickly starts making you a drink.
    Philip: (slightly annoyed) Here’s the virgin drink for the virgin.
    Narrator: He slides a bright red Shirley Temple across the bar toward you, complete with cherry and little umbrella, shaking his head and muttering about “soft city folk.”
    Narrator: You sit down, slightly humiliated, the pub suddenly seeming smaller or maybe that’s just you.

Narrator: As you settle into the stool, your eyes wander across the pub.

Narrator: The place is narrow, dimly lit, and chaotic in that oddly charming way only an Aussie dive can be.

Narrator: Crooked fairy lights snake along the walls, boomerangs hang at slightly alarming angles, and a small shrine to Steve Irwin dominates one corner.

Narrator: Surrounding it are several dried, dead stingrays, carefully arranged, giving the display a slightly macabre edge.

Narrator: The bar is in a state of organized chaos. Bottles of wine, spirits, and Philip’s questionable concoctions are all stacked together, some empty, each labeled in his scrawled, broken English you can’t even make out a word. 

Narrator: Coasters are scattered across the sticky bar, and the air carries the faint tang of spilled booze. 

Narrator: Far down the bar, the only other patron sits hunched over his glass. Bald, glasses, and wearing a black pork pie hat…

Narrator: A gas mask dangles from his neck, swinging slightly as he leans forward, staring into his drink as if lost in some very deep thought.

Narrator: Philip returns after briefly speaking with the other patron, wiping his hands on a dirty rag, and leans on the counter.

Philip: Crikey… you’re the first person I’ve seen come through that door.

Philip: I had one of me boys come and weld it shut a coupla years back now.

Philip: Guess the time and rain finally got to that bugga. All me regulars stick with the Bilco doors out back.

Player: (still in pain) I’ll have to remember that for next time… Because goddamn, did that hurt.

Philip: (shaking his head slightly) Aye, had to get it shut though, mate. Too many crack and heroin addicts kept sneaking in through that alley.

Narrator: Philip picks up a glass nearby and starts to clean it with his dirty rag, making the glass more cloudy as he “cleans it”.

Philip: Ruined the place more times than I care to count. Once I sealed it, those drongo addicts were finally gone for good.

Philip: But this leads me to my next problem…

Narrator: You realize this is turning out to be quite a long story all because of that damn door. Now you’re wondering when and how it will end.

Philip: With the front entrance stuck in that alley and the only other way in through the Bilco doors out back, not many people know this place even exists, mate!

Philip: Sooo.. I had the idea to try and shift my business onto the computer digital space! I had enough to get some ad space on a coupla platforms, but…

Philip: I had to all the marketing myself… which turned out okay. I’ve got a coupla regulars now.

Narrator: Philip’s expression starts to sour slightly as he’s in thought.

Philip: But crikey… They’re some weird blokes.

Narrator: Desperate to change the subject to anything other than his business and financial failings, you want to try asking him about something.

Player: Do you mind if I ask you a question, Philip?

Philip: (grinning, shrugging a little) Go ahead, mate! What’s on your mind?

Dialogue Choices For Interaction 2:

Choice 1(-,☠️): Ask about the other patron
Player: So what’s the deal with the bloke over there?
Philip: (frowing slightly) Ah… 
Philip: Well… 
Narrator: The guy at the end of the bar is now giving Philip a death stare.
Philip: (voice cracking, nervously) Ya, see here mate… he’s someone who GREATLY appreciates his… 
Narrator: You noticed Philip’s gaze shift to something behind you.
Philip: (squeaks, fearfully) Privacy.
Narrator: You start to turn around…
Narrator: BBAAMMMM!!!
Narrator: You just took a right hook the face! Stunning you into a short daze. 
Narrator: You then hear someone shouting right in your face.
Tweaker Patron: (muffled) WHERE IS HE!?!
Narrator: Philip is completely pale and locked in place.
Narrator: The tweaker patron grabs your collar with both hands and starts shaking you uncontrollably.
Tweaker Patron: (less muffled) WHERE’S JESSE!?!
Narrator: You’ve been shaken back to a conscious state and are now completely terrified.
Player: (high pitched, scared) THE FUCK ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT!?!
Narrator: The tweaker patron starts stepping back towards the sealed door you forced open for them earlier.
Narrator: He snatches up his gas mask and straps it on with terrifying efficiency
Tweaker Patron: (frantic) WE NEED TO COOK!!!
Narrator: The tweaker patron bolts out and you and Philip try to process what in the hell just happened.
Player: PHILIP! WHAT THE FUCK WAS THAT!
Philip: (annoyed) I told ya! My regulars are some weird blokes but at least they aren’t drongo addicts!
Narrator: You’ve just about had it with this pub at this point… 
Narrator: You had basically forced your way in, which led to you hurting your back.
Narrator: Now you were just punched in the face for no reason other than asking a simple question… 
Narrator: Which you really never even got a response to.
Narrator: Now it looks like Philip has got something to say to you.
Philip: (turning red, muttering through gritted teeth) Bloody hell… and out goes one of the regulars!
Philip: (annoyed) Thanks a lot, mate. Couldn’t just keep to yourself, could ya…
Narrator: A feeling of murderous rage starts to fill within you, all the events leading to this moment feel like scars in your mind.
SUB CHOICE (PASS/FAIL)
Choice 1(⚪): Remain Calm, Carry On!
Narrator: You remember why you’re really here and push the anger deep down.
Choice 2(☠️): CRASH OUT!
Narrator: You dump what’s left in your glass on Philip’s head, and he’s left in complete shock by your actions.
Philip: (pissed, serious) What in the hell do ya think you’re doing…
Philip: (sharply) MATE!
Narrator: He gets into a fighting stance and quickly jabs you in the nose, knocking you back a few feet.
Player: (loud, bellowing) RRRRRAAAAAAAAHHHHHH!!!
Narrator: Your rageful roar echoes throughout the bar and into the alley. Philip’s face starts to turn pale from the fear of what he’s just awakened.
Philip: (timidly) O.. O.. Okay, mate. I’m sorry.. I apologize.
Narrator: You start to calm down for just a second…
Narrator: But Philip opens his mouth again.
Philip: I mean, mate. What’d you expect? You dumped your drink on me so I had to set ya straight.
Philip: (smirking, under his breath but audible) Not that you’d be able to take me anyway.
Narrator: Just as he finished that line, you take the glass still in your hand and huck it straight into Philip’s face.
Narrator: He’s stunned, and his nose starts to trickle some blood.
Narrator: A voice screams in your mind…
Narrator: FINISH HIM!
Narrator: You grab Philip and drag him over the bar and onto the floor.
Narrator: You then hop up on top of the bar and perform a devastating elbow drop right into Philip’s solar plexus.
Narrator: You feel the impact knock all the air out of Philip’s lungs and hear two distinct noises. CRACK. SQUISH.
Narrator: You get up and slowly realize what you’ve done… 
Narrator: You check Philip’s pulse..
Narrator: Nothing…
Player: OH… SHIT!!
Narrator: Realizing you’ve just committed murder, you start a life on the run from authorities. After stealing what little cash the bar had in the register, you drift from place to place.
Narrator: In the end you died while you were asleep in a snowstorm as a homeless beggar in a remote region of the world.
[GAME OVER: MURDERER]

Choice 2(+): Ask about the sign out front
Player: So… what’s with the sign out front? 
Player: The one with Kim Jong Un and the chickens?
Philip: (brightening instantly) Ohhh, that beauty! Yeah, me and me blokes designed that. I put that up ’cause I bloody love that man.
Player: (concerned) …Kim Jong Un?
Philip: Aye! Little fella looks like a fat baby. Absolutely adorable.
Philip: I just wanna pinch those cheeks of his.
Player: …Which cheeks?
Philip: (already inhaling to answer, eyes widening with enthusiasm) Well, if ya mean—
Player: Hold on… Never mind, please don’t answer that.
Player: You do know he’s a totalitarian dictator who doesn’t feed his people but instead publicly executes them and puts them into forced labor camps?
Narrator: Philip is visibly stunned by your words.
Philip: Oh… 
Philip: I thought he was just a famous fat chinese influencer…
Philip: (timidly, quietly) This is what I get for dropping out in highschool.
Philip: (sadly, teary-eyed) Probably yet another reason why the bar is failing.


Choice 3(+): Ask about the Steve Irwin shrine
Player: So what’s the story with the Steve Irwin shrine?
Player: It’s a little out there… no?
Narrator: Philip glances over at the candles, the photos, and the ring of dried dead stingrays. His eyes well up with tears.
Philip: (choked up) Beautiful, ain’t it? Finest part of the whole bloody bar.
Philip: Built it meself… Every piece, every candle, every photo.
Philip: (a singular tear runs down his cheek) Real proper tribute… for a proper man.
Player: It’s beautiful… How’d you get the dead stingrays, though?
Philip: (regaining his composure) Oh, those?
Philip: (proudly) Caught ‘em meself while I was out fishing. Every single one of the buggers.
Philip: Took me weeks to dry ‘em out just right. Was worth it, though. Really gives it character
Philip: (sadly) Course, not everyone is such a big fan of it as I am.
Philip: Got this one regular, some nasty old cat lady… A real piece of work. She says the shrine is ‘grotesque’ and ‘deeply troubling’.
Narrator: Philip’s expression dims.
Philip: (quiet, defeated) Probably another reason the bar’s failing…

Narrator: In this moment you are given a fateful choice…

Narrator: Lend a hand to Philip and give some good advice to try and turn his bar in the right direction.

Narrator: Or…

Narrator: Tell Philip to start anew. He’s better off finding another job and ending this black hole of a business.
===
